      "title": "At least four people killed in Japan as typhoon Dujuan triggers heavy rain, landslides",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/typhoon-dujuan-japan-latest-weather-millions-told-to-evacuate-tokyo",
      "description": "<p>Rescuers search for missing in collapsed homes after storm causes landslides, travel chaos and power outages</p><p>Typhoon Dujuan has killed at least four people and injured 22 in Japan, while tens of thousands of houses near Tokyo remained without power after the storm swept through the region, authorities said on Tuesday.</p><p>Dujuan – which <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/sep/21/weather-tracker-japan-typhoon-dujuan\">brought violent winds of 144km/h (89mph)</a> – was moving away from Japan on Tuesday morning, allowing authorities to downgrade most heavy rain and landslide warnings.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/22/typhoon-dujuan-japan-latest-weather-millions-told-to-evacuate-tokyo\">Continue reading...</a>",
